{
  "_comment": [
    "Stored-XSS regression corpus for render.SanitizeArtifactHTML (aihub#240, resolves #144).",
    "Categories track the five classes enumerated in the render-refactor research doc",
    "01-static-html-render-engine-research.md 2.6 'SVG 专属安全清单', plus style_block, which",
    "was added after two consecutive review rounds found the sanitizer bypassable there and",
    "nowhere else -- the corpus had zero cases in the one place the code actually failed.",
    "external_resource carries protocol-relative (//host) forms as well as scheme forms:",
    "the three scheme cases all passed while //host slipped through the same regex branch,",
    "so the category guard reported coverage the class did not have.",
    "",
    "Each case asserts on the SANITIZER output only. The sandboxed iframe and the CSP header",
    "are separate, independent layers -- a payload that survives sanitization is still expected",
    "to be inert in a browser, but defence in depth means we do not rely on that here.",
    "",
    "forbidden: substrings that must NOT appear in the sanitized output (case-insensitive).",
    "required:  substrings that MUST survive -- these guard against over-sanitizing, which is",
    "           its own failure mode: a policy that eats legitimate SVG silently breaks every",
    "           complex diagram (see acceptance criterion 4)."
  ],
